WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
In 2008, just 4.9 per
cent of British retail

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.150
sales were made online.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.450
By 2025, it was 27.5 per cent,

4
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.280
more than five times as big a share.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.820
Online, every shopper can
compare every price in seconds.

6
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.270
And the biggest retailers seem
to stock almost everything.

7
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.990
So how can a tiny online shop
survive against giants like that?

8
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.770
In this mission, you'll
use a graph lab to test

9
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.400
what a price comparison site
does to a shop's revenue.

10
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.770
Then you'll meet a sales
curve with a very long tail,

11
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.100
and see why it matters online.

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.930
Your mission: find out
how a small firm can

13
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.360
compete when buyers can
see every rival's price.
